/-!
# Actual smooth rapidly decreasing coefficient families

The original Haar Fourier coefficients of a smooth family satisfy
compact-uniform summable bounds for all real base-derivative words and
all polynomial frequency weights. The condition is preserved by
addition, complex constant multiplication, real base differentiation,
the exact coordinate Fourier multipliers, and arbitrary fixed joint
base/torus directional differentiation.
Every weighted derivative word is also pointwise absolutely summable.

This coefficient package makes no infinite-series smoothness or
relative cohomology assertion.
-/
